Boost your foraging experience with a detailed tooltip that breaks down all modifiers affecting your search radius.

[h2]Key Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Detailed Modifier Breakdown:[/b] Shows exact effects of weather, darkness, exhaustion, traits, skills, and other factors on your search radius.
[*] [b]Persistent Radius Display:[/b] Shows current search radius next to the eye icon (optional, toggle in Mod Options).
[*] [b]Min/Max Indicators:[/b] Highlights when search radius reaches game limits.
[/list]

[h2]Mod Options[/h2]
Customize under [b]Menu -> Options -> Mods -> Foraging Tooltip Extended[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Show Radius before Eye Icon:[/b] Toggle persistent radius display (default: enabled)
[*] [b]Tooltip Value Alignment:[/b] Choose right or left alignment for tooltip values (default: right)
[/list]

[h2]Why I Made This[/h2]
I've always enjoyed foraging as a reliable source of food and medical herbs since the early days of Project Zomboid. However, Build 42's vanilla tooltip felt confusing — for example, Weather Effect appeared as both a red negative value at the top and a green negative value in the bonuses section. This dual representation made it unclear how modifiers actually interact.

I couldn't find any working mods for Build 42 that addressed this, so I created this mod to make foraging mechanics transparent and understandable.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Supported builds: 42.15+ (tested on 42.20.2 SP & MP)
[*]Safe to add/remove mid-game
[*]Compatible with most mods unless they modify the "Vision Effectiveness" tooltip.
[*]Recommended with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3593442524]Quick Forage Icon Discard [B42][/url]
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Found a bug or have suggestions? Leave a comment! I'd love to hear your thoughts and improve the mod further.
